      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1e0040fae9e26decbc46e7f801036a78bde1b196054c4590765fc65d0cf4293b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completion is a representation change that makes reflection visible: family-specific conductor and archimedean factors produce completed L-functions, while for zeta the pole-cleared xi normalization and the theta-Mellin calculation exhibit a concrete source of the symmetry. In neither representation does reflection alone force critical-line or real zeros.",
