      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2c5ce592c7652fb69e19d7a5ec98f38a27f15c98390cdc9157272a7fd3454279",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite polynomial analogues separate reflection symmetry from root confinement. A symmetry-preserving transform and modular period-polynomial encoding both expose reflected polynomial geometry, but period-polynomial results require additional factorwise inequalities or a phase-transparent exponential model with uniform perturbation control, while the C=3 recurrence passes through heuristic steps with no zero-stability theorem.",
