    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_32e97bc7b0034658c2d30361f754e399e8a295524a0afae8c44034a2001a9beb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Two distinct preprocessing steps precede meaningful zero comparison in the cited automorphic settings: remove level-inherited oldforms to isolate newforms with their own normalized Euler products, then unfold the zeros of a chosen primitive standard L-function by its local density. Provenance isolation and density normalization preserve different information and should not be conflated.",
