      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A finite zero certificate couples local detection with an independently computed total count. Sign changes or a separate locator produce candidate critical-line zeros, while an argument-principle or Turing count supplies the conserved integer; equality certifies completeness only in the bounded window.",
