    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4f49cff8a2ed7b083da8b624f974d3148c212f311ee1689ebbb4dfcbfceb0da1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A reflected functional rule is weaker than an L-function interface. Fractional differentiation of zeta introduces a branch-sensitive noninteger phase and logarithmic coefficient weights that are not multiplicative, blocking the classical Euler-product route to primes; the automorphic proposal instead retains local factors, archimedean completion, and contragredient duality while leaving global continuation as a separate analytic obligation.",
